inates of the vectors of $B$ relative to the basis $C.$ \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to C}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ -7 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186350961 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "595fd527-e8fd-5360-87f1-acbeab511566" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Change-of-Coordinates Matrix Given a Linear Connection Between Two Bases"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d5e1d546-417f-5e35-97b9-a386c4ed9493" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350963} {:answer/id #uuid "ae71ea26-09e2-5495-bfe6-b093749392f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350964} {:answer/id #uuid "588c7143-8332-5c6d-a392-1a0c1863d550" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350965} {:answer/id #uuid "d6e61cf0-4c99-5dc9-8464-20d27c4bea14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350966} {:answer/id #uuid "65d0f2e1-094e-57c8-bcb6-196486545ec7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350967}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d6e61cf0-4c99-5dc9-8464-20d27c4bea14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350966} :answer-field/id #uuid "08279880-7f5f-5c81-8da5-37fb8a6a6520" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350962}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7ee07384-0d2d-5d34-baac-3296201157fd" :question/math-academy-id "q-35795" :question/problem "Let $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ and $C={{c}_{1},{c}_{2}}$ be bases of ${R}^{2}.$ \nFind the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{C\\to B}$ from $C$ to $B$ given that\n\n$$\n[{c}_{1}]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,[{c}_{2}]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The change-of-coordinates matrix from $C$ to $B$ is a matrix whose respective columns are the coordinates of the vectors of $C$ relative to the basis $B.$ \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n{P}_{C\\to B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124831 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "23b6a85e-e1de-590c-84d2-379052b1b9f3" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Invertibility Property of the Change-of-Coordinates Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "802c32d5-200e-57b5-b136-227740e3bfa2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 3 \\\\ -7 & -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122009} {:answer/id #uuid "9d4e381e-da75-5e74-9e9c-a3391a5c5f71" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 7 \\\\ 3 & -5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122010} {:answer/id #uuid "472db7aa-9e2f-5042-a922-3dba61445603" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 3 \\\\ -7 & 5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122011} {:answer/id #uuid "49e2de5a-38c3-55b3-8e74-a4de4b4ca09e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -5 \\\\ 4 & 7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122012} {:answer/id #uuid "6b3f0a84-127b-57de-a732-c93d89d954ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -7 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122013}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6b3f0a84-127b-57de-a732-c93d89d954ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -7 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122013} :answer-field/id #uuid "687b3ca8-e3d6-5649-8e48-2f44b3197bae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122008}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "51bd98dc-1e1e-5c5c-9609-7609b0be859e" :question/math-academy-id "q-35799" :question/problem "The change-of-coordinates matrix from the basis $C$ to the basis $B$ is given by\n${P}_{C\\to B}=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 7 \\\\ -3 & -4\\end{aligned}].$ Find the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C$  ." :question/worked-solution "The change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C$ is the inverse of the change-of-coordinates matrix from $C$ to $B.$ Therefore, we simply need to find the inverse of the given matrix.\n\nComputing the inverse of ${P}_{C\\to B}$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{B\\to C} & ={P}_{C\\to B}^{-1} \\\\  & ={[\\begin{aligned}5 & 7 \\\\ -3 & -4\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5\\cdot (-4)-7\\cdot (-3)}[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -7 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =1\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-4 & -7 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -7 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186350968 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "595fd527-e8fd-5360-87f1-acbeab511566" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Change-of-Coordinates Matrix Given a Linear Connection Between Two Bases"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "018520cb-0b91-59cf-bd9a-4ee49d5d024b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 \\\\ 5 & -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350970} {:answer/id #uuid "390f07a5-69f0-5c34-bb06-2ed7dd00cb33" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350971} {:answer/id #uuid "27806874-ad81-5e9a-a8ea-cb595de4ffdf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350972} {:answer/id #uuid "b18a3934-e264-57ea-891a-157bb438fe25" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 & -4 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350973} {:answer/id #uuid "21f2f5cd-5193-5bd8-8972-76b8a57391ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5 \\\\ 2 & -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350974}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "018520cb-0b91-59cf-bd9a-4ee49d5d024b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 \\\\ 5 & -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350970} :answer-field/id #uuid "c1d52d88-3570-5410-8b58-b9a43a691d97" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350969}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "605e4ee1-9076-5716-842a-05787d15c730" :question/math-academy-id "q-36355" :question/problem "Let $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ and $C={{c}_{1},{c}_{2}}$ be bases of ${R}^{2}.$ If ${b}_{1}=5{c}_{2}-3{c}_{1}$ and ${b}_{2}=2{c}_{1}-4{c}_{2},$ find the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{B\\to C}$ from $B$ to $C.$" :question/worked-solution "The coordinates of the vectors in $B$ relative to the basis $C$ are\n\n$$\n[{b}_{1}]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\\,[{b}_{2}]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C$ is a matrix whose respective columns are the coordinates of the vectors of $B$ relative to the basis $C.$ \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to C}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 \\\\ 5 & -4\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124891 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6b973d79-8fe4-5033-8202-9693004855dc" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Change-of-Coordinates Matrix When One of the Bases is the Standard Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "918ee8b8-0471-5b56-9d4a-d1bea72a1798" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122369} {:answer/id #uuid "e9fa9047-f7e8-5f9d-9949-d7729255d727" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ -3 & -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122370} {:answer/id #uuid "137fcdf5-5430-5185-9456-e37560c66253" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122371} {:answer/id #uuid "2c9c852b-8ae9-5e00-8520-24a9937f102d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122372} {:answer/id #uuid "5849b7d5-8611-5d5c-9543-42b26d93c84b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122373}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "137fcdf5-5430-5185-9456-e37560c66253" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122371} :answer-field/id #uuid "c99babbf-598a-548e-8170-a53c9365a613" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122368}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b7561091-5a13-5f20-989c-89982f4b4b54" :question/math-academy-id "q-36366" :question/problem "Let $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ be a basis of ${R}^{2}$ and let $S$ be the standard basis of ${R}^{2}.$ \nFind the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{B\\to S}$ from $B$ to $S$ if \n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall  that the standard basis of ${R}^{2}$ consists of the vectors ${e}_{1}$ and ${e}_{2},$ given by\n\n$$\n{e}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{e}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe components of the vectors of $B$ are just the coordinates relative to the standard basis:\n\n$$\n[{b}_{1}]_{S}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,[{b}_{2}]_{S}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $S$ is a matrix whose respective columns are the coordinates of the vectors of $B$ relative to the basis $S.$ \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to S}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186350975 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f989cbaf-2d99-5267-8864-48a48db2d535" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Change-of-Coordinates Matrix Between Two Bases"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fca9a934-c8d2-5fd2-8f37-9ba92b1a2200" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}7 & -5 \\\\ -3 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350977} {:answer/id #uuid "ef65e3ec-0962-5c12-a4ba-e04d5e6e0ee9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 7 \\\\ 3 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350978} {:answer/id #uuid "258b39bb-3fff-5639-9639-476f2ff16150" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}7 & -3 \\\\ -5 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350979} {:answer/id #uuid "f35007ce-eb95-5f09-a3c5-70122190c7c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 & -5 \\\\ -3 & 7\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350980} {:answer/id #uuid "87bebe9d-bb37-5824-94ce-fe561aa6bfeb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}7 & 5 \\\\ 3 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350981}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fca9a934-c8d2-5fd2-8f37-9ba92b1a2200" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}7 & -5 \\\\ -3 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350977} :answer-field/id #uuid "b9baefe1-4b3c-5235-930f-8be9fc5bbeca" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350976}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f7e547d0-2041-562b-9514-c21517672564" :question/math-academy-id "q-36398" :question/problem "Let $B={[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}]}$ and $C={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}]}$ be bases of ${R}^{2}.$ Find the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ and $C$ as ${{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ and ${{c}_{1},{c}_{2}}$, respectively.\n\nThe change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C$ is a matrix whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors of $B$ relative to the basis $C.$\n\nHence, we need to find the coordinates of ${b}_{1}$ and ${b}_{2}$ relative to the basis $C.$ We can do this simultaneously by considering the matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}| & | & | & | \\\\ {c}_{1} & {c}_{2} & {b}_{1} & {b}_{2} \\\\ | & | & | & |\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we simply reduce the left-hand side to reduced row-echelon form using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -2 & 4 \\\\ -3 & -8 & 3 & -9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-3){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 7 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the right-hand side, we obtain the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to C}=[\\begin{aligned}7 & -5 \\\\ -3 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124897 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6b973d79-8fe4-5033-8202-9693004855dc" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Change-of-Coordinates Matrix When One of the Bases is the Standard Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8707931a-c194-580c-b511-71b3002cce5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a=-3,$ $b=-1,$ and $c=1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350983} {:answer/id #uuid "a65fa8c8-b293-5439-b328-e91efd5210d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a=-3,$ $b=0,$ and $c=0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350984} {:answer/id #uuid "afedde8d-b22a-5542-a98f-a95d0b2a436f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a=0,$ $b=0,$ and $c=1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350985} {:answer/id #uuid "51838c0c-76b4-5801-8336-657301c3426b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a=-3,$ $b=0,$ and $c=4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350986} {:answer/id #uuid "ff9d8e30-30be-5668-bdd7-5775269ce64f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a=-5,$ $b=4,$ and $c=1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350987}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8707931a-c194-580c-b511-71b3002cce5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a=-3,$ $b=-1,$ and $c=1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350983} :answer-field/id #uuid "24ee64ba-ad92-516e-8d6b-61f4c26f68c8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350982}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "62a8923e-9667-58a1-b193-1a3c8d5a2238" :question/math-academy-id "q-36400" :question/problem "Let $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}}$ be a basis of ${R}^{3}$ and let $S$ be the standard basis of ${R}^{3}.$ What are the values of $a,b,$ and $c$ if \n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nand the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $S$ is \n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to S}=[\\begin{aligned}a & -5 & 0 \\\\ 4 & b & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & c\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall  that the standard basis of ${R}^{3}$ consists of the vectors ${e}_{1},{e}_{2},$ and ${e}_{3},$ given by\n\n$$\n{e}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{e}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{e}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe components of the vectors in $B$ are just the coordinates relative to the standard basis:\n\n$$\n[{b}_{1}]_{S}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,[{b}_{2}]_{S}=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,[{b}_{3}]_{S}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $S$ is a matrix whose respective columns are the coordinates of the vectors of $B$ relative to the basis $S.$ \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to S}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -5 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, $a=-3,$ $b=-1,$ and $c=1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186350988 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6b973d79-8fe4-5033-8202-9693004855dc" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Change-of-Coordinates Matrix When One of the Bases is the Standard Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dfc74b44-b8cb-5743-ba22-a0231e1d9641" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 7 \\\\ -3 & -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350990} {:answer/id #uuid "78b458bf-c099-5ec8-94b2-2a75e69824a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & -7 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350991} {:answer/id #uuid "b89a8d5d-2282-57e6-b817-861f04ebfaf5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}7 & -2 \\\\ -4 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350992} {:answer/id #uuid "7bc0b5b5-1d53-5747-ac95-dfcd76757a24" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 \\\\ 7 & -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350993} {:answer/id #uuid "560867dc-8a4f-5e51-8b96-8a2d62246b84" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 7 \\\\ -3 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350994}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dfc74b44-b8cb-5743-ba22-a0231e1d9641" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 7 \\\\ -3 & -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350990} :answer-field/id #uuid "023f0a61-5c7f-5d5f-a943-aaffc7317c8b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350989}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c0e29690-0559-5609-84c1-8e332dcb9ec7" :question/math-academy-id "q-36401" :question/problem "Let $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ be a basis of ${R}^{2}$ and let $S$ be the standard basis of ${R}^{2}.$ \nFind the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{B\\to S}$ from $B$ to $S$ if \n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall  that the standard basis of ${R}^{2}$ consists of the vectors ${e}_{1}$ and ${e}_{2},$ given by\n\n$$\n{e}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{e}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe components of the vectors of $B$ are just the coordinates relative to the standard basis:\n\n$$\n[{b}_{1}]_{S}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,[{b}_{2}]_{S}=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $S$ is a matrix whose respective columns are the coordinates of the vectors of $B$ relative to the basis $S.$ \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to S}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 7 \\\\ -3 & -4\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125144 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "595fd527-e8fd-5360-87f1-acbeab511566" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Change-of-Coordinates Matrix Given a Linear Connection Between Two Bases"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5ea0c4f3-1e05-5470-8cd8-dd0eeb6171e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a=2,$ $b=0,$ and $c=-1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350996} {:answer/id #uuid "e0d66b45-d311-57d5-a579-57d3ce9e115f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a=1,$ $b=2,$ and $c=0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350997} {:answer/id #uuid "2bb6a4cc-77a9-50c2-890f-6edc6e787bf8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a=2,$ $b=2,$ and $c=5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350998} {:answer/id #uuid "10083b74-9a6b-5628-adf9-195d10c95ddf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a=1,$ $b=-2,$ and $c=5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350999} {:answer/id #uuid "acd781c9-b081-584d-80c5-450b97be0c05" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a=0,$ $b=2,$ and $c=-1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351000}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2bb6a4cc-77a9-50c2-890f-6edc6e787bf8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a=2,$ $b=2,$ and $c=5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350998} :answer-field/id #uuid "c6e0f0d3-94f4-5e48-87de-a537f60aba76" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350995}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8ff70514-6088-5578-a352-2d83d0571687" :question/math-academy-id "q-81394" :question/problem "Let $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}}$ and $C={{c}_{1},{c}_{2},{c}_{3}}$ be bases of ${R}^{3}.$ \nWhat are the values of $a,b,$ and $c$ if \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} & ={c}_{1}+2{c}_{2}-{c}_{3}, \\\\ {b}_{2} & =5{c}_{3}+2{c}_{2}, \\\\ {b}_{3} & ={c}_{2}-{c}_{1},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand  the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C$ is\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to C}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ a & b & 1 \\\\ -1 & c & 0\\end{aligned}]?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The coordinates of the vectors in $B$ relative to the basis $C$ are\n\n$$\n[{b}_{1}]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,[{b}_{2}]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\\,[{b}_{3}]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C$ is a matrix whose respective columns are the coordinates of the vectors of $B$ relative to the basis $C.$ \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to C}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 5 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, $a=2,$ $b=2,$ and $c=5.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351001 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "595fd527-e8fd-5360-87f1-acbeab511566" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Change-of-Coordinates Matrix Given a Linear Connection Between Two Bases"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eaa80bed-64be-5ebb-b39d-08253db29def" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a=-1,$ $b=4,$ and $c=3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351003} {:answer/id #uuid "362505ae-3f7b-5ec2-9688-6f11f5c6bbb5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a=3,$ $b=4,$ and $c=0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351004} {:answer/id #uuid "48ba82e7-861b-50dc-a6a2-c74700beab56" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a=3,$ $b=0,$ and $c=3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351005} {:answer/id #uuid "63749493-2e3b-5cd8-9a84-f48b14beb613" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a=1,$ $b=-5,$ and $c=2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351006} {:answer/id #uuid "aad49c0b-3b5e-53dc-971d-624ed8ef78be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a=-1,$ $b=0,$ and $c=0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351007}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eaa80bed-64be-5ebb-b39d-08253db29def" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a=-1,$ $b=4,$ and $c=3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351003} :answer-field/id #uuid "7953d339-0fdf-52f1-8dba-62f7b1861982" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351002}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cebf33a6-1e88-5dcd-a020-6375d9d328e4" :question/math-academy-id "q-81825" :question/problem "Let $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}}$ and $C={{c}_{1},{c}_{2},{c}_{3}}$ be bases of ${R}^{3}.$ \nWhat are the values of $a,b,$ and $c$ if \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} & =3{b}_{3}-{b}_{1}+{b}_{2}, \\\\ {c}_{2} & =4{b}_{2}-5{b}_{1}, \\\\ {c}_{3} & =2{b}_{1}+3{b}_{3},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand  the change-of-coordinates matrix from $C$ to $B$ is\n\n$$\n{P}_{C\\to B}=[\\begin{aligned}a & -5 & 2 \\\\ 1 & b & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 & c\\end{aligned}]?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The coordinates of the vectors in $C$ relative to the basis $B$ are\n\n$$\n[{c}_{1}]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,[{c}_{2}]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,[{c}_{3}]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe change-of-coordinates matrix from $C$ to $B$ is a matrix whose respective columns are the coordinates of the vectors of $C$ relative to the basis $B.$ \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n{P}_{C\\to B}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -5 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, $a=-1,$ $b=4,$ and $c=3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351008 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6b973d79-8fe4-5033-8202-9693004855dc" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Change-of-Coordinates Matrix When One of the Bases is the Standard Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6cdee27f-9ce7-5f65-9310-00235c8fcbfd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a=7,$ $b=0,$ and $c=0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351010} {:answer/id #uuid "f20bc0fc-dae5-5839-aa1f-0095d12ea376" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a=0,$ $b=7,$ and $c=0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351011} {:answer/id #uuid "0a50abd6-68bc-5a72-ae10-d9c84f5e9dfa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a=1,$ $b=-2,$ and $c=0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351012} {:answer/id #uuid "1eec352b-5f82-5d59-9239-abfc9b93e0bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a=7,$ $b=0,$ and $c=-1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351013} {:answer/id #uuid "de6422b9-fb6e-50a4-962f-67a0961cfc43" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a=0,$ $b=3,$ and $c=-3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351014}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6cdee27f-9ce7-5f65-9310-00235c8fcbfd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a=7,$ $b=0,$ and $c=0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351010} :answer-field/id #uuid "1549485a-6e21-5c6c-862f-712d2c5729f1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351009}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "38cd5032-0982-5775-aa3b-320af45a4643" :question/math-academy-id "q-81848" :question/problem "Let $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}}$ be a basis of ${R}^{3}$ and let $S$ be the standard basis of ${R}^{3}.$ What are the values of $a,b,$ and $c$ if \n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nand the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $S$ is \n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to S}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & a & -3 \\\\ b & -2 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 3 & c\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall  that the standard basis of ${R}^{3}$ consists of the vectors ${e}_{1},{e}_{2},$ and ${e}_{3},$ given by\n\n$$\n{e}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{e}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{e}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe components of the vectors in $B$ are just the coordinates relative to the standard basis:\n\n$$\n[{b}_{1}]_{S}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,[{b}_{2}]_{S}=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,[{b}_{3}]_{S}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $S$ is a matrix whose respective columns are the coordinates of the vectors of $B$ relative to the basis $S.$ \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to S}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, $a=7,$ $b=0,$ and $c=0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351015 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "23b6a85e-e1de-590c-84d2-379052b1b9f3" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Invertibility Property of the Change-of-Coordinates Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "81b9ab77-0001-5089-aec4-a85f211cf78c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}7 & -3 \\\\ -5 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351017} {:answer/id #uuid "132af5d6-6d6d-5cf4-9bf9-b85df2ddfb14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 5 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351018} {:answer/id #uuid "fb847658-a4a1-57ff-b9b1-05e4283c0304" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 5 \\\\ 3 & -7\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351019} {:answer/id #uuid "6413f290-5947-5976-8302-4d1e7f480cab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ 5 & -7\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351020} {:answer/id #uuid "98f47a94-3132-59b4-a324-02655d9b23cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 3 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351021}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "98f47a94-3132-59b4-a324-02655d9b23cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 3 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351021} :answer-field/id #uuid "d74aef95-23c7-561a-91b7-d26a9642e6aa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351016}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9db820e8-979e-5ad9-a435-5d7032f9f097" :question/math-academy-id "q-81856" :question/problem "The change-of-coordinates matrix from the basis $B$ to the basis $C$ is given by \n${P}_{B\\to C}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 7\\end{aligned}].$ \nFind the change-of-coordinates matrix from $C$ to $B$  ." :question/worked-solution "The change-of-coordinates matrix from $C$ to $B$ is the inverse of the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C.$ Therefore, we simply need to find the inverse of the given matrix.\n\nComputing the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to C}$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{C\\to B} & ={P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} \\\\  & ={[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 7\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\cdot 7-3\\cdot 5}[\\begin{aligned}7 & -3 \\\\ -5 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}7 & -3 \\\\ -5 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 3 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351022 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "23b6a85e-e1de-590c-84d2-379052b1b9f3" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Invertibility Property of the Change-of-Coordinates Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8dc626ae-1bb3-5139-9bd2-751e53c31c90" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & \\frac{2}{3} \\\\ -3 & \\frac{5}{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351024} {:answer/id #uuid "821a47fe-2241-5663-abdf-44737bb0b741" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ -\\frac{2}{3} & -\\frac{5}{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351025} {:answer/id #uuid "6784958c-6ac6-560a-823f-0ee0dbea6d96" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{3} & \\frac{2}{3} \\\\ -3 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351026} {:answer/id #uuid "606c4c35-7a79-5725-a5b9-4c3b21af8d0f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{3} & -\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351027} {:answer/id #uuid "e10afd59-ca25-51d6-9643-40fa5e0969e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ 3 & \\frac{5}{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351028}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e10afd59-ca25-51d6-9643-40fa5e0969e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ 3 & \\frac{5}{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351028} :answer-field/id #uuid "6605da92-18e2-5173-abef-1b3a400a78f8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351023}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a27a3c1e-ad3c-56e4-aa1a-d2aedbc7058d" :question/math-academy-id "q-81859" :question/problem "The change-of-coordinates matrix from the basis $C$ to the basis $B$ is given by\n${P}_{C\\to B}=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 \\\\ -9 & -3\\end{aligned}].$ Find the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C$  ." :question/worked-solution "The change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C$ is the inverse of the change-of-coordinates matrix from $C$ to $B.$ Therefore, we simply need to find the inverse of the given matrix.\n\nComputing the inverse of ${P}_{C\\to B}$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{B\\to C} & ={P}_{C\\to B}^{-1} \\\\  & ={[\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 \\\\ -9 & -3\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5\\cdot (-3)-2\\cdot (-9)}[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -2 \\\\ 9 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-3 & -2 \\\\ 9 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ 3 & \\frac{5}{3}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
